From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Cast in Quick Settings (ADR-034)

One Cast tile lists every screen org.projectluma.Cast1 finds, whatever it
speaks (Google Cast, Miracast, AirPlay): pinned, then recent, then nearby,
with "Connects directly" and "Higher delay" where they apply. Discovery runs
only while the menu is open (StartDiscovery/StopDiscovery), and the list
follows DevicesChanged without reshuffling.

Choosing a screen opens its sheet: Entire screen, Use as a separate screen,
One display (with several monitors) or One app (a window picker; the app is
presented floating on the wallpaper), Optimize for the screen or this
computer, and Sound on the screen or this computer, remembered per screen.
While casting the same sheet changes what is shared or where sound plays with
Session.Change, without reconnecting, and Stop Casting always works. The
shelf gets a Cast island (connecting, reconnecting, the screen's name) with
its own menu.

Pairing uses one dialog for CodeRequested: enter the code shown on the TV,
show a code to type on the TV, or accept on the TV. Errors are the service's
codes in the Shell's words, with Try Again and Other Screens.

Privacy the Shell alone can enforce:
- Before a system modal with a password entry (polkit, keyring, network
  secrets, unlock) is painted, the Shell calls Session.SetPrivacyCurtain and
  holds the dialog's paint until the service answers; no answer in time stops
  the cast. The curtain is lowered when the dialog closes.
- While casting, and with org.projectluma.cast silence-notifications on,
  banners are silenced as runtime state only; show-banners is never written.
  A monitor in CapturedConnectors shows no banner at all, critical or not.
- The service ends casts on lock; the Shell shows why once.

Adds js/ui/lumaCast.js (the one D-Bus client), lumaCastSheet.js,
lumaCastDialogs.js, status/cast.js, luma-cast.css and the luma-cast icons;
hooks panel.js, sessionMode.js, shelf.js, messageTray.js, lumaGrid.js
(RoundedPreview for picker thumbnails) and introspect.js (window list for the
service). Without luma-cast installed the tile stays hidden.

Generated against the Shell .81 build tree (0117-0120) for release .82.
